{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe planner must be compared with legacy decisions before it gains authority. Preview consumers require the existing mutation array and canonical hash to remain stable while lifecycle intent data is additive and versioned.\n\n## Outcome\nRun `TicketPlan` generation in shadow, compare its mutations/dispositions with legacy output, and add a versioned lifecycle-intents preview section that old consumers can ignore.\n\n## Plan\n1. Feed the same frozen observation to legacy differ and shadow planner. Fail tests on unexplained mutation or disposition divergence and name approved deltas.\n2. Extend preview/manifest rendering with an ADDITIVE versioned lifecycle-intents section under a new top-level key, leaving every existing key and the mutation array bytes untouched. Preserve the existing mutation array bytes and `serialize_manifest` canonical hash exactly.\n3. Ensure construction, check, dry-run, and shadow modes perform zero repository saves, ticket writes, Jira calls, or subprocess launches.\n4. Add golden fixtures covering normal, deferred dependency, filtered, tombstoned, and partial-snapshot plans.\n\n## Impacted sites (existing construction/consumer surface)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/manifest_renderer.py` — `render_plan` / `render_dry_run_or_strict` / `render_throttle`: gain ONE additive top-level `lifecycle_intents` section keyed off the shadow `ticket_plans`; the existing mutation array and every existing key are emitted byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_planning.py:167` — the consumer that lazy-loads the renderer (`renderer_mod = _load_manifest_renderer()`): passes the shadow plans through to the renderer additively; no existing behavior changes.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mutation.py` — `serialize_manifest` (the canonical mutation-array manifest + sha256): NOT modified; a golden test pins its bytes/hash to prove the additive section does not perturb it.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/ticket_planner.py` — pure `plan_pass` shadow plans are the parity source; a new PURE parity helper compares shadow mutations/dispositions against the legacy mutation list and returns named deltas (zero I/O).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py:285` — the shadow construction site (`ctx.observation, ctx.ticket_plans = ticket_planner.plan_pass(...)`): stays a pure, additive, effect-free shadow attach; parity comparison reads `ctx.mutations` (legacy) vs `ctx.ticket_plans` (shadow) without writes.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_ticket_plan_shadow.py` — held-out oracle extended with parity + additive-section + byte-stability + zero-I/O golden tests.\n\n## Testing\nGolden and poison tests pin old fields/hashes, the additive section, parity diagnostics, and zero I/O.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Shadow mutations match legacy behavior for the ticket-sourced corpus except explicitly named approved deltas.\n- [x] Shadow dispositions match legacy behavior for the ticket-sourced corpus except explicitly named approved deltas.\n- [x] Preview preserves the existing mutation array bytes exactly.\n- [x] Preview preserves the existing `serialize_manifest` canonical hash exactly.\n- [x] Preview adds one versioned lifecycle-intents section that legacy consumers may ignore.\n- [x] Construction, check, dry-run, and shadow paths perform zero repository/provider/subprocess writes.\n- [x] A parity failure identifies the ticket identity, the observation version, and the differing plan fields, with no unbounded or secret content.\n\n## Out of scope\nProduction coordinator authority remains RP-03 S3."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787620949320910001,"uuid":"94b39c78-9931-4695-9d2c-3086783dca42"}